// Settings: the surface that had fourteen controls and no checks at all.
//
// # Why these count menu entries instead of naming one
//
// Every control here opens a dropdown, and **not one menu entry has an
// accessible name**: every menuitem row ends at `content=` with nothing after
// it. `PaintsNamed` cannot be written for any of them, because there is no name
// to match. A menu a screen reader cannot announce is a menu nobody can use
// without sight, and it is the same defect that leaves 70 buttons unreachable.
//
// # Why PaintsMore and not a count of the tree
//
// The menus are retained. Across four consecutive opens the tree grew
// 32 -> 34 -> 38 -> 43 -> 49 menuitems and never shrank, because a closed menu is
// laid out at 0x0 rather than removed. A tree count therefore rises whether or
// not the control did anything. Painted entries are stable: 0 with every menu
// closed, 6 with one open.
//
// # settings-agent-menu fails, and the control is fine
//
// It reports `6 -> 2`: fewer entries painting after the press than before, which
// is what pressing a control looks like while another menu is already open. It
// fails identically run alone on a freshly restored profile, so the open menu
// comes from its own arrival step. Driven by hand from a clean surface the
// control is correct, 0 painting before and 2 after. Left failing on purpose:
// deleting it hides the arrival bug, and a `Holds` would let a genuinely broken
// dropdown pass.
//
// # Not covered
//
// `Refresh`, `Stop` and `Re-check` act on the update channel, so their outcome is
// a network round trip needing a store assertion rather than a geometry one.
// Three further controls open native macOS file panels, which cannot be driven.
[
    (
        id: "settings-language-menu",
        group: "settings",
        what: "the language control opens a menu",
        open: Some("Settings"),
        hover: None,
        click: Some("Current language: English"),
        subject: "menuitem",
        expect: PaintsMore,
    ),
    (
        id: "settings-agent-menu",
        group: "settings",
        what: "the default agent control opens a menu",
        open: Some("Settings"),
        hover: None,
        click: Some("Default agent"),
        subject: "menuitem",
        expect: PaintsMore,
    ),
    (
        id: "settings-effort-menu",
        group: "settings",
        what: "the default effort control opens a menu",
        open: Some("Settings"),
        hover: None,
        click: Some("Default effort"),
        subject: "menuitem",
        expect: PaintsMore,
    ),
    (
        id: "settings-permission-menu",
        group: "settings",
        what: "the default permission control opens a menu",
        open: Some("Settings"),
        hover: None,
        click: Some("Default permission"),
        subject: "menuitem",
        expect: PaintsMore,
    ),
]
